  "id": "occasion-setting",
  "term": "occasion setting",
  "definition": "Occasion setting is a form of Pavlovian learning in which one stimulus signals whether another stimulus will lead to a particular outcome. In other words, it helps an organism use the surrounding situation to resolve when a cue does or does not predict what will happen next.",
